I stop at a large fruit and vegetable stall.
There is a lot of fruit and vegetables there.
A sign shows the price for the apples.
A kilo costs two euros fifty.
"What would you like?" the seller asks.
"Good morning," I say.
"I would like five apples."
"Gladly," the seller says.
He takes five nice apples.
He weighs the apples.
"That makes three euros twenty," he says.
"Will you take anything else?"
"No, thank you, that is all," I answer.
I give him five euros.
He gives me the change.
I put the apples into my shopping bag.
Then I go to the next stall.
